WEBVTT

1
00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:49.958


2
00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:52.000
<b>Arjun has become helpless.</b>

3
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.083
<b>He has already said that he sees</b>
<b>no good in this war.</b>

4
00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:58.041
<b>And here,</b>

5
00:00:58.041 --> 00:01:02.875
<b>Sanjay now tells Dhritarashtra</b>
<b>what happened next.</b>

6
00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:04.083
<b>Sanjay says</b>

7
00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:07.625
<b>that now, the scorcher of foes, Arjun, simply said,</b>

8
00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:10.125
<b>"I will not fight."</b>

9
00:01:10.125 --> 00:01:14.375
<b>Saying this, he fell completely silent.</b>

10
00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:15.333
<b>And there,</b>

11
00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:20.833
<b>Lord Sri Krishna, looking at Arjun like this,</b>
<b>only smiles softly</b>

12
00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:24.208
<b>and then begins to say something to Arjun...</b>

13
00:01:24.208 --> 00:01:25.541
<b>What he will say</b>

14
00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:28.458
<b>is described in the next verses.</b>

15
00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:33.375


16
00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:37.916
<b>Here, Arjun's despair finally reached its peak,</b>

17
00:01:37.916 --> 00:01:40.208
<b>where he just said that</b>

18
00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:42.958
<b>he will not fight this war anymore </b>

19
00:01:42.958 --> 00:01:45.250
<b>and fell silent.</b>

20
00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.416
<b>You know that</b>

21
00:01:46.416 --> 00:01:49.041
<b>Dhritarashtra was longing for this very thing, </b>

22
00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:51.000
<b>that Arjun would abandon the war</b>

23
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.416
<b>and his son Duryodhana would be victorious.</b>

24
00:01:54.416 --> 00:01:59.208
<b>To put a pause on this very desire of</b>
<b>Dhritarashtra, these growing hopes,</b>

25
00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:04.291
<b>Sanjay here addresses Arjun with</b>
<b>the epithet Parantapa.</b>

26
00:02:04.291 --> 00:02:05.125
<b>Parantapa</b>

27
00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:10.625
<b>means the one who gives pain to his enemies,</b>
<b>the one who destroys them.</b>

28
00:02:10.625 --> 00:02:13.291
<b>It's as if Sanjay wants to say,</b>

29
00:02:13.291 --> 00:02:14.750
<b>"O my King,</b>

30
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:20.208
<b>do not assume from Arjun's words that</b>
<b>victory belongs to Duryodhana.</b>

31
00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:24.208
<b>Arjun has the full capability</b>
<b>to destroy his enemies.</b>

32
00:02:24.208 --> 00:02:27.250
<b>And yet, not everything has happened;</b>

33
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.041
<b>do not be pleased so quickly."</b>

34
00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:31.625
<b>Sanjay also knows</b>

35
00:02:31.625 --> 00:02:33.833
<b>that dharma should win,</b>

36
00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:34.583
<b>and</b>

37
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:36.125
<b>will win.</b>

38
00:02:36.125 --> 00:02:40.000
<b>Meanwhile, here, Sri Krishna only smiles.</b>

39
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.125
<b>The smile on his lips</b>

40
00:02:42.125 --> 00:02:44.625
<b>is the smile of an all-knowing one.</b>

41
00:02:44.625 --> 00:02:51.000
<b>That all-knowing one who knows</b>
<b>what will happen, when, and how.</b>

42
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.333
<b>Nothing is beyond his knowledge.</b>

43
00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.208


44
00:03:00.208 --> 00:03:07.750
<b>The same Gandiva, the mere lifting of which</b>
<b>used to instill a surging energy in Arjun,</b>

45
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.416
<b>has been relinquished by him.</b>

46
00:03:12.416 --> 00:03:16.125
<b>The war for which preparations had</b>
<b>been going on for so long, </b>

47
00:03:16.125 --> 00:03:24.000
<b>for which his brothers, his companions,</b>
<b>his army, all stand ready</b>

48
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:30.083
<b>Arjun has now asked to abandon this very war.</b>

49
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:32.333
<b>Arjun knew everything</b>

50
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:33.958
<b>who the war was against,</b>

51
00:03:33.958 --> 00:03:39.083
<b> and who would support Duryodhana.</b>

52
00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:42.625
<b>And until now, the war hasn't even begun,</b>

53
00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:47.875
<b>not a single arrow has been shot, not</b>
<b>a single weapon has been raised.</b>

54
00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:52.375
<b>Nothing has changed yet.</b>

55
00:03:52.375 --> 00:03:53.541
<b>Then why</b>

56
00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:58.125
<b>such an adverse change,</b>
<b>in a great warrior like Arjun? </b>

57
00:03:58.125 --> 00:04:00.750
<b>such weakness?</b>

58
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:05.708
<b>How does one become so weak? </b>

59
00:04:05.708 --> 00:04:08.625
<b>Something has indeed changed,</b>

60
00:04:08.625 --> 00:04:10.583
<b>but</b>

61
00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.916
<b>not externally.</b>

62
00:04:12.916 --> 00:04:17.416
<b>What has changed, has changed from within.</b>

63
00:04:17.416 --> 00:04:22.791
<b>The cancerous disease of thoughts.</b>

64
00:04:22.791 --> 00:04:26.000
<b>What is a cancerous disease?</b>

65
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.500
<b>In our body,</b>

66
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:32.333
<b>In our body, new cells are</b>
<b>constantly proliferating, taking birth.</b>

67
00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:36.041
<b>And this all happens under control.</b>

68
00:04:36.041 --> 00:04:36.958
<b>But</b>

69
00:04:36.958 --> 00:04:38.166
<b>sometimes,</b>

70
00:04:38.166 --> 00:04:42.875
<b>when some abnormal cells</b>
<b>start growing uncontrollably,</b>

71
00:04:42.875 --> 00:04:49.166
<b>their quantity becomes so high</b>
<b>that even life comes under threat. </b>

72
00:04:49.166 --> 00:04:51.125
<b>Similarly,</b>

73
00:04:51.125 --> 00:04:55.583
<b>if only negative thoughts keep taking birth,</b>

74
00:04:55.583 --> 00:04:58.791
<b>their quantity becomes so high that,</b>

75
00:04:58.791 --> 00:05:00.333
<b>like a cancerous disease,</b>

76
00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:06.291
<b>that quantity destroys your</b>
<b>ability to think/understand.</b>

77
00:05:06.291 --> 00:05:09.458
<b>In such a situation,</b>
<b>the human mind becomes weak.</b>

78
00:05:09.458 --> 00:05:13.541
<b>Willpower dies.</b>

79
00:05:13.541 --> 00:05:17.416
<b>Beware of this cancerous disease of thoughts.</b>

80
00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:21.458
<b>Most of our thoughts are merely imagination,</b>

81
00:05:21.458 --> 00:05:22.666
<b>not truth.</b>

82
00:05:22.666 --> 00:05:27.083
<b>Don't admit defeat by falling</b>
<b>into this imagination.</b>

83
00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:33.250
<b>Just the awareness of when thoughts</b>
<b>start dominating you is sufficient.</b>

84
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.958
<b>Once awareness comes,</b>

85
00:05:34.958 --> 00:05:37.958
<b>solutions will also be found,</b>

86
00:05:37.958 --> 00:05:40.875
<b>control over thoughts will also come.</b>

87
00:05:40.875 --> 00:05:42.541
<b>Through counseling,</b>

88
00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:43.791
<b>through meditation,</b>

89
00:05:43.791 --> 00:05:45.000
<b>through rest,</b>

90
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.416
<b>there are many more remedies.</b>

91
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.250


92
00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.583
<b>Arjun is breaking down here,</b>

93
00:05:54.583 --> 00:05:55.875
<b>and I am</b>

94
00:05:55.875 --> 00:05:58.541
<b>smiling.</b>

95
00:05:58.541 --> 00:06:04.208
<b>From my smile, I hope you haven't mistaken</b>
<b>me as cruel, have you?</b>

96
00:06:04.208 --> 00:06:07.416
<b>This is by no means a mockery of Arjun.</b>

97
00:06:07.416 --> 00:06:11.250
<b>I have immense affection for him;</b>

98
00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:15.875
<b>how could I mock him?</b>

99
00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:18.916
<b>This smile is only because,</b>

100
00:06:18.916 --> 00:06:26.000
<b>in the face of crisis, in the face of worries,</b>
<b>man begins to consider himself so helpless.</b>

101
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:32.791
<b>If there is life, then crises will come,</b>
<b>worries will arise.</b>

102
00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:38.041
<b>But man gives these crises even more strength</b>

103
00:06:38.041 --> 00:06:40.250
<b>with his sorrow,</b>

104
00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:44.041
<b>his helplessness.</b>

105
00:06:44.041 --> 00:06:45.833
<b>You tell me,</b>

106
00:06:45.833 --> 00:06:49.833
<b>what will work in any situation</b>

107
00:06:49.833 --> 00:06:52.625
<b>continuing to lament about it</b>

108
00:06:52.625 --> 00:06:53.791
<b>or</b>

109
00:06:53.791 --> 00:06:57.166
<b>trying to solve it?</b>

110
00:06:57.166 --> 00:07:01.875
<b>But who knows how many times we</b>
<b>just get stuck in lamentation.</b>

111
00:07:01.875 --> 00:07:06.833
<b>We forget to smile.</b>

112
00:07:06.833 --> 00:07:09.916
<b>And we also forget that</b>

113
00:07:09.916 --> 00:07:15.125
<b>you have already faced</b>
<b>many difficult situations,</b>

114
00:07:15.125 --> 00:07:20.416
<b>you have reached here today</b>
<b>after coming out of many crises.</b>

115
00:07:20.416 --> 00:07:24.666
<b>Now just think for a moment,</b>

116
00:07:24.666 --> 00:07:26.750
<b>in that past time,</b>

117
00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.916
<b>you felt the same, didn't you?</b>

118
00:07:28.916 --> 00:07:31.750
<b>that this crisis will not pass,</b>

119
00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.500
<b>but it did pass.</b>

120
00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:37.291
<b>If the coming of crises is destiny,</b>

121
00:07:37.291 --> 00:07:41.583
<b>then their passing is also destiny.</b>

122
00:07:41.583 --> 00:07:45.041
<b>And if the difficulty will pass anyway,</b>

123
00:07:45.041 --> 00:07:48.041
<b>then why lament for it,</b>

124
00:07:48.041 --> 00:07:53.625
<b>why not face it with a smile?</b>

125
00:07:53.625 --> 00:07:58.375
<b>Those who understand destiny</b>
<b>like this do not grieve;</b>

126
00:07:58.375 --> 00:08:00.875
<b>they smile.</b>

127
00:08:00.875 --> 00:08:04.791
<b>And your smile is also contagious.</b>

128
00:08:04.791 --> 00:08:05.833
<b>From you,</b>

129
00:08:05.833 --> 00:08:08.000
<b>it spreads in your family,</b>

130
00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.958
<b>spreads in society.</b>

131
00:08:09.958 --> 00:08:12.375
<b>It gives them strength too.</b>

132
00:08:12.375 --> 00:08:13.791
<b>Life is beautiful.</b>

133
00:08:13.791 --> 00:08:16.166
<b>Everything will be fine</b>

134
00:08:16.166 --> 00:08:19.125
<b>if you keep walking properly.</b>

135
00:08:19.125 --> 00:08:20.541
<b>Smile, won't you?</b>

136
00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:25.250


137
00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.250
<b>In professional life,</b>

138
00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.208
<b>you must have often seen this happen.</b>

139
00:08:30.208 --> 00:08:32.833
<b>Someone is making a mistake,</b>

140
00:08:32.833 --> 00:08:35.333
<b>and if you give them the right advice,</b>

141
00:08:35.333 --> 00:08:38.208
<b> show them the proper path,</b>

142
00:08:38.208 --> 00:08:40.916
<b>people take offense.</b>

143
00:08:40.916 --> 00:08:41.750
<b>But</b>

144
00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:45.708
<b>this was to help them, wasn't it?</b>

145
00:08:45.708 --> 00:08:49.500
<b>Then why such a reaction?</b>

146
00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:55.125
<b>If you pour more water into</b>
<b>a pot filled to the brim,</b>

147
00:08:55.125 --> 00:08:57.041
<b>what will happen?</b>

148
00:08:57.041 --> 00:09:01.375
<b>Will that pot be able to accept that water?</b>

149
00:09:01.375 --> 00:09:02.916
<b>No, right?</b>

150
00:09:02.916 --> 00:09:04.875
<b>Similarly,</b>

151
00:09:04.875 --> 00:09:11.583
<b>many people are so full of their own thoughts,</b>
<b>their own perspectives,</b>

152
00:09:11.583 --> 00:09:14.083
<b>that there is no room left</b>

153
00:09:14.083 --> 00:09:15.791
<b>for any new perspective,</b>

154
00:09:15.791 --> 00:09:19.125
<b>any new suggestion.</b>

155
00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:21.958
<b>Until the pot is empty,</b>

156
00:09:21.958 --> 00:09:25.541
<b>it will not accept water.</b>

157
00:09:25.541 --> 00:09:26.541
<b>In the same way,</b>

158
00:09:26.541 --> 00:09:31.750
<b>until a person is ready to</b>
<b>acquire new knowledge,</b>

159
00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:35.458
<b>every effort will fail.</b>

160
00:09:35.458 --> 00:09:37.375
<b>Before giving any advice,</b>

161
00:09:37.375 --> 00:09:40.041
<b>before showing a new path,</b>

162
00:09:40.041 --> 00:09:42.166
<b>find out if</b>

163
00:09:42.166 --> 00:09:45.541
<b>that person is ready at this time</b>

164
00:09:45.541 --> 00:09:46.750
<b>or not.</b>

165
00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.416
<b>And if not,</b>

166
00:09:48.416 --> 00:09:52.000
<b>wait for the right time.</b>

167
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:52.708
<b>Yes,</b>

168
00:09:52.708 --> 00:09:56.666
<b>if it's an emergency situation, you can't wait.</b>

169
00:09:56.666 --> 00:09:57.791
<b>In such cases,</b>

170
00:09:57.791 --> 00:10:02.958
<b>you may have to give immediate suggestions</b>
<b>or take control.</b>

171
00:10:02.958 --> 00:10:03.708
<b>But</b>

172
00:10:03.708 --> 00:10:05.000
<b>usually,</b>

173
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:08.375
<b>it's best to wait for the right time.</b>

174
00:10:08.375 --> 00:10:14.416
<b>It is said that the teacher appears</b>
<b>only when the student is ready.</b>

175
00:10:14.416 --> 00:10:18.250
<b>This is something like that.</b>

176
00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:21.916
<b>Arjun has now surrendered,</b>

177
00:10:21.916 --> 00:10:24.833
<b>his pot has become empty,</b>

178
00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:26.666
<b>now the time has come</b>

179
00:10:26.666 --> 00:10:32.250
<b>when he is completely ready</b>
<b>to receive knowledge.</b>

